  "articleBody": "Ever wonder why prospective clients in nearby towns aren't finding your business, even though you serve them? It's often down to how your service areas are set up, especially for AI search. Traditional SEO focused on keywords, but AI systems look for structured, reliable information about your business, including where you actually operate. If your service area information is vague or incorrect, AI engines like Google AI Overviews or Siri might just skip over you, recommending a competitor with a clearer profile. AI systems crave clarity and consistency to confidently recommend you, and that includes your geographical reach.\n\n### What Can Change the Right Choice\n\nWhen defining your service areas, think about how Google and other AI systems understand location. Google allows you to define service areas by cities or postal codes, with a limit of 20 areas. Trying to define a service area by a radius is a common mistake and won't work. Your overall service area should also realistically be within about a two-hour driving distance from your main business base. If you try to cast too wide a net or use virtual offices without actual staffing, AI systems might see inconsistencies, which reduces their confidence in recommending you. Understanding these parameters is key to making sure your business shows up where it needs to.\n\n### Common Mistakes to Avoid\n\nMany businesses make simple but impactful mistakes when setting up their service areas. Creating separate profiles for every city you serve, especially if you don't have eligible physical locations in each, is a big no-no. Listing a virtual office that isn't truly staffed during business hours also raises red flags. Another common error is leaving your public address visible when you primarily serve customers at their location, which can confuse both customers and AI. And resist the urge to keyword-stuff your business name with locations; AI systems are smarter than that. Focus on accuracy and consistency. If you have multiple locations or a hybrid storefront/service-area model, professional guidance can be invaluable to avoid these pitfalls and ensure your profile is optimized for AI discovery.\n\n### What to Do Next\n\nIf you suspect your service area settings are holding you back, it's a good idea to review your Google Business Profile with these insights in mind. Ensure your listed cities and postal codes are accurate and realistic. Consider whether your address should be hidden if you're a service-area business. A clean, accurate profile is your best bet for AI visibility. For help making sure your service area optimization is on point, especially if you have a complex setup, contact AI Visibility Solutions. We can help clarify your profile to make sure AI systems confidently recommend you to local prospects.",
  "datePublished": "2026-09-30"
